chapter.v:
	Having then 

	 gifts differing according to the grace that is given to us, let us use them: if prophecy, let us prophesy in proportion to our faith;
 [2 Thess. 1:10; 1 Tim. 2:6; 2 Tim. 1:8; Rev. 1:2]

	or ministry, 

	 let us use it in our ministering; he who teaches, in teaching;
 [Luke 17:30; Rom. 8:19, 23; Phil. 3:20; Titus 2:13; [2 Pet.]

	Be kindly 

	 affectionate to one another with brotherly love, in honor giving preference to one another;
 [2 Cor. 13:11;]

	rejoicing in 

	 hope, patient in tribulation, continuing steadfastly in prayer;
 [Matt. 3:8-10;]
